  "title": "Ranavalona I",
  "summary": "Ranavalona I ruled Madagascar from 1828, when she was proclaimed queen on 1 August after her husband Radama I died, until her death on 16 August 1861. Gale describes persecution of Malagasy Christians from 1836 and restrictions on Europeans; EBSCO says she tried to oust all foreigners and outlawed Christianity, and civil war followed. Her son succeeded as Radama II.",
